WEBVTT

NOTE Edited transcription of a historical recording. Unclear speech is marked; use current specifications for ordering.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Welcome! Today we will be covering appliance
panels in WW Wood Products cabinetry. We'll

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.200
walk through the types of panels available, how
they're designed and ordered, and some

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.200
important tips to avoid common mistakes.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.100
Appliance panels are custom-sized panels
designed to cover built-in and integrated
appliances,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:31.600
like refrigerators, ice makers, dishwashers,
warming drawers, and beverage centers.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.400
These panels can match either a full overlay or
inset door and drawer style, and are designed

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.200
according to the appliance manufacturer's
specifications.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.800
It's important to remember that the dealer is
responsible for requesting the correct

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.200
sizing.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.600
Here we see an example of an inset refrigerator
panel.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.600
This style gives a clean, flush look, matching
the surrounding cabinetry, while concealing

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.400
the appliance.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.600
There are several types of appliance panels
available.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.500
REF Standard Refrigerator Panel.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.700
IREF Inset version of the refrigerator panel
with a face frame and door.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.800
BCF Beverage Center Fronts for Glass Front
Coolers.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.700
DP Dishwasher Panel.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.100
IDP Inset Dishwasher Panel with Frame and Door.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.200
Each is designed for specific applications, so
it's important to choose the right one

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.400
for your project.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.000
panels. Available in standard and inset options,
each door of the appliance would have its

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.900
own panel. For example, a French door
refrigerator would likely need three panels, one
for the

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:41.300
left door, one for the right, and a third for
the bottom freezer drawer. All refrigerator

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:46.700
panels are priced per square inch. Panels 47
inches high or taller will likely have

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.900
at least one horizontal rail for support.
However, many custom options are available

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:57.100
with a custom quote. When placing an order, you
must include the appliance specs or provide

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:02.400
the manufacturer make and model number. If
needed, doors will be mounted on a quarter-inch

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.600
backer panel with an eighth-inch spacer. Keep in
mind, no custom grooving, notching,

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:14.200
or drilling on the backs of the panels are
available. However, ice maker or water dispenser

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.600
cutouts are available at $200 list price for
each cutout.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.500
Beverage Center Fronts BCF Beverage center
fronts are 3-quarters inch

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.500
thick door frames specifically designed for
glass front beverage coolers.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.500
They're available up to 24 inches wide and 80
inches tall.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.800
When ordering, specify both width and height,
along with the door style and rail and style

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.900
widths.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:42.300
Custom rail widths can be done except on miter
door styles.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:48.700
Note, the Metro Door Style, in all finishes
except painted MDF, will also require an
aluminum

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.900
trim to finish along the inside edge of the
cutout.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.400
The trim is available in matte black, silver, or
matte brass.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.500
Dishwasher Panels, DP and IDP.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.200
Dishwasher panels are for paneled dishwashers
only.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.500
Specify the door style when ordering.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.800
No custom grooving, notching, or drilling is
available on the back of these panels.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:15.700
When using IDP panels, remember that Shiloh face
frames are 30.5 inches high, not 30 inches.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.100
As long as your panel matches the height of a
standard base cabinet, you can select bridge

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.100
door options at no additional charge.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:29.600
For other design options, please request a
custom quote from quotes@wwinc.com.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.900
Here's an example of an inset DP panel with a
custom top drawer and lower door in an inset

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.100
frame.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.600
This specific detailing required a custom quote,
but you can see how it offers a more

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:46.500
attractive design that coordinates better with
the neighboring cabinets.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.200
Mistakes to avoid One of the most common
mistakes is overlooking

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.700
appliance depth.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.400
Always double-check that the panel's front
aligns with neighboring cabinets.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.300
Sometimes you may need to make surrounding
cabinets deeper, or pull them out from the

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.900
wall to create a flush look.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.600
Examples of appliance panels Here we have some
examples.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.100
The picture on the left shows a REF refrigerator
panel and a DP dishwasher panel in Eclipse

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.800
frameless cabinetry using the Metro Door style.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.800
The picture on the right shows two Shiloh Inset
IREF panels.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.600
Notice there are no horizontal rails despite the
large panel size.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.000
For similar custom detailing, a quote is
required.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.200
Appliance panels are located in the accessories
section of both Eclipse and Shiloh spec books.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:37.700
You can find interactive digital copies on the
dealer portal at my.wwinc.com.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.900
To customize the design of any of the panels,
please remember to request a custom quote

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.700
from quotes@wwinc.com.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:51.100
Additionally, visit shilohcabinetry.com and
eclipsecabinetry.com for gallery images and

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.200
more inspiration.
